Do you have the physical reach to grab the object?

05:11.820 --> 05:12.220
Exactly.

05:12.220 --> 05:15.860
Or if you're a software microservice, is the database connection open?

05:16.300 --> 05:19.880
Can you physically execute the SQL query over the network?

05:20.400 --> 05:22.900
And if the answer is yes, the action is in the F set.

05:23.040 --> 05:23.280
Right.

05:23.380 --> 05:28.040
Which is just a subset of U, the total universal space of all conceivable actions.

05:28.540 --> 05:28.780
Okay.

05:28.840 --> 05:31.720
So you establish physical capability with F.

05:31.720 --> 05:36.960
Then we move inward, right, to the C set, which is relational validity.

05:37.140 --> 05:38.440
Yes, relational validity.

05:38.620 --> 05:40.460
This is where the governing relations come in.

05:40.580 --> 05:46.080
It asks, out of the actions that are physically feasible, which ones actually satisfy the governing

05:46.080 --> 05:48.280
roles or the safety protocol?

05:48.400 --> 05:50.020
Or the relational roles assigned to the actor.

