or if the safety rule actively blocked it, which is a Type II relational failure requiring them to wait for the pressure to drop.

12:09.920 --> 12:10.400
Exactly.

12:11.020 --> 12:13.780
The remedy for a Type I failure is more resources.

12:14.340 --> 12:14.940
Fix the button.

12:14.940 --> 12:19.940
The remedy for a Type II failure is changing the rules or waiting for the right conditions.

12:20.580 --> 12:24.120
If you collapse F and C, you get uninformative failures.

