Okay.

12:46.940 --> 12:48.420
Here's where it gets really interesting.

12:48.620 --> 12:51.380
This leads us directly into parts four and five of the paper.

12:51.980 --> 12:55.440
The epistemic gap between observation and distributed knowledge.

12:55.560 --> 12:55.720
Yes.

12:55.780 --> 13:03.640
So we have an action that is physically feasible, and it's perfectly valid under the rules, but the actor cannot prove it.

13:04.500 --> 13:06.100
Let's say with a chemical reactor example.

13:06.280 --> 13:06.520
Okay.

13:06.520 --> 13:11.840
Well, the technician has a pressure gauge, but it's a really coarse, low-resolution sensor.

13:12.060 --> 13:15.060
It only reads two states, nominal and elevated.

