21:11.260 --> 21:12.980
The domain applications are massive.

21:13.440 --> 21:15.000
Let's look at security and authentication.

21:15.700 --> 21:20.100
Flixing shows us that just because a credential exists doesn't automatically mean an action is authorized.

21:20.760 --> 21:23.620
Identity is not evidence, and evidence is not commitment.

21:23.840 --> 21:24.000
Right.

21:24.080 --> 21:24.780
There are separate layers.

21:25.080 --> 21:26.220
What about autonomous agents?

21:26.220 --> 21:36.460
For AI, separating the actuators, which is feasibility, from the safety constraints, validity from the perception establishability, and finally from the planning commitment makes AI auditable.

21:37.000 --> 21:39.640
If a drone crashes, you know exactly which layer failed.

21:40.020 --> 21:40.280
Wow.

21:40.780 --> 21:42.360
And scientific reasoning too, right?

21:42.560 --> 21:42.920
Yes.

21:43.600 --> 21:45.860
An observation does not entail an inference.

21:46.280 --> 21:48.800
An inference doesn't entail a warranted result.

21:49.140 --> 21:52.160
And a warranted result doesn't entail that you should act on it.

21:52.160 --> 21:59.560
So to bring this all together for the listener to take into their own work, there are four final design principles mandated by the text.

21:59.860 --> 22:00.600
Let's run through them.

22:00.680 --> 22:02.580
Principle one, preserve the boundaries.

22:02.940 --> 22:06.360
Never collapse F, C, K, and A.

22:07.080 --> 22:13.680
Explicitly design your systems to separate physical capability from relational rules from certifiable evidence.

22:14.000 --> 22:16.920
Principle two, design for relevant distinguishability.

22:17.100 --> 22:19.200
Only partition what needs different treatment.

22:19.200 --> 22:22.960
Engineer your data equivalence classes to match your rule variance.

22:23.100 --> 22:27.360
Principle three, change the evaluation position when local inference isn't enough.

22:27.780 --> 22:29.420
Build composite observer patterns.

22:29.740 --> 22:33.220
Bring the evidence together mathematically before you ask if the rules are satisfied.

22:33.380 --> 22:35.640
And principle four, make history explicit.

22:35.920 --> 22:38.040
Because history determines future rules.

22:38.580 --> 22:43.780
Your architecture must dynamically re-evaluate the governing relation after every single action.

22:44.100 --> 22:44.520
Incredible.

